  "rules": [
    "When recent history shows a downtrend followed by a sharp spike (e.g., Example 2-4), the model exhibits severe upward bias and fails to capture immediate mean reversion; correct forecasts by applying a negative adjustment factor of -15% to -20% on the first 7 days post-spike.",
    "The model consistently underestimates volatility during high sentiment periods (e.g., Example 5), producing artificially flat paths that ignore sudden reversals; increase forecast variance or apply a random walk correction when sentiment history contains mixed positive/negative signals within a 3-day window.",
    "In scenarios where the last 18 days show consolidation near support levels, the model over-smooths price action and ignores potential breakout failures; reduce the initial forecast target by 5-10% if the first 3 historical days are below the moving average.",
    "The model demonstrates a systematic lag in reacting to sentiment shifts; when sentiment turns positive after a downtrend, delay the upward adjustment by 2-3 days relative to the true outcome trajectory."
  ]
